Digging around, I found this flash description. http://www.uiowa.edu/% 
7Eacadtech/phonetics/

Use the German section, then click "Frikative" to get x and h; use  
Spanish then click "fricativas" to get X x and h; use American  
English and click "fricative" to get h. Unfortunately, the  
descriptions of what your mouth is doing are in German, Spanish and  
English respectively, so most folks won't be able to read everything.

This site shows X as the sound I was (incorrectly) describing as  
trilled, which epkat uses in jbocradi.

